From 32e754a6bd2e8012db59486295e5e7ffe0f2aa49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 09:03:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] enforce home budgets for placement-refused cards

Why: a hub-homed pool card was filtered before lane admission, while the
leasing worker correctly skipped home-owned budget decisions. Neither
machine could stop the cumulative spending loop.

Reuse the lane's no-progress/spend decisions for placement-refused ready
and review rows on each admitted dispatch tick. Preserve foreign-copy
ownership, dry-run behavior, per-card exemptions, locked state checks and
the existing spend-decision producer. No new watcher, timer or budget.

Both entry paths reach kanban_db_dispatch.dispatch_once:
gateway/kanban_watchers_dispatcher.py _dispatch_board calls it; CLI
hermes_cli/kanban_ops.py cmd_dispatch calls it too.

Proof: regression first on main: 3 failed / 3 passed, with absent holds
for ready/review spend and remote no-progress. After fix: 67 tests passed
across regression and existing budget suites. scripts/check: 21 checks OK.
Read-only hub census found one unique home-owned over-budget ready card:
26 spending runs, 37,686,039 cache-read tokens, zero budget-triaged events.

Known limit: a worker can lease between ready and the home's next tick,
allowing at most one extra run per episode. Existing scheduling admission
and drain gates are unchanged.
